ibes the number of rectangles to the total number of shapes?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434577 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2cf3ec40-81c7-5457-9357-3212d8b07109" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434577 #edb/ref 1074 "We count the number of rectangles. We see that there is $1$ rectangle.\n\n We count the total number of shapes. We see that there are $6$ shapes in total.\n\nSo the ratio of rectangles to the total number of shapes is $\\frac{1}{6}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434578 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186434576 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434578 #edb/ref 1069 "q-92980" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434578 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434578 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/2e/2eb4a8fee0c9d2c28058685035ee14991a9df55f5128749614e5797f1a144b1b.png)\n\nIf the ratio of rhombuses to triangles is $\\frac{2}{\\boxed{}},$ what is the missing number?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434578 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "31bf28dd-407a-5a25-aa7a-11f90a52be84" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434578 #edb/ref 1074 "We count the number of rhombuses. We see that there are $2$ rhombuses.\n\nWe count the number of triangles. We see that there are $3$ triangles.\n\nHence, the ratio of rhombuses to triangles is $\\frac{2}{3}.$\n\nSo the missing number is $3.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434579 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186434566 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434579 #edb/ref 1069 "q-60169" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434579 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434579 #edb/ref 1071 "What is missing in the following sentence?\n\nA drink contains $9$ fluid ounces of pure lemon juice and $13$ fluid ounces of clean water, so there are $\\boxed{}$ fluid ounces of pure lemon juice for each fluid ounce of distilled water." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434579 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "3a44dfd7-a851-5f83-a265-ef0532428a91" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434579 #edb/ref 1074 "The ratio of the fluid ounces of pure lemon juice to the fluid ounces of clean water is  $9:13.$ \n\nWe can rewrite this ratio as a fraction, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{9}{13}\n$$\n\nThis means that there are $\\frac{9}{13}$ fluid ounces of pure lemon juice for each fluid ounce of clean water." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434580 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186434574 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434580 #edb/ref 1069 "q-60257" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434580 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434580 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/b1/b14906ddfde919b60d119d9250ae47ff295d549f757c2a687d6796d09eb661ef.png)\n\nIf the ratio of pentagons to total shapes is $\\frac{4}{\\boxed{}}$ then what is the missing number?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434580 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "48d22e7d-f957-5ae6-a0ae-ac363856d52f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434580 #edb/ref 1074 "We count the number of pentagons. We see that there are $4$ pentagons.\n\n We count the total number of shapes. We see that there are $7$ shapes.\n\nHence, the ratio of pentagons to total shapes is$\\frac{4}{7}$\n\nSo the missing number is $7.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434581 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186434568 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434581 #edb/ref 1069 "q-92947" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434581 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434581 #edb/ref 1071 "From left to right, what are the missing numbers in the following sentence?\n\nTo prepare some hot chocolate, $\\frac{3}{10}$ kilograms of crushed chocolate is required for each liter of milk. Therefore, this hot chocolate has a ratio of $\\boxed{}$ kilograms of crushed chocolate to $\\boxed{}$ liters of milk." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434581 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "81652f70-e2b3-55e8-9631-e7e6684fbb2d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434581 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's rewrite the fraction $\\frac{3}{10}$ as a ratio:\n\n$$\n3:10\n$$\n\nTherefore, the hot chocolate has a ratio of $3$ kilograms of crushed chocolate to $10$ liters of milk." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434582 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186434567 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434582 #edb/ref 1069 "q-60240" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434582 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434582 #edb/ref 1071 "What is missing in the following sentence?\n\nTo make green paint, Victor mixed $6$ pints of blue paint and $5$ pints of yellow paint, so there are $\\boxed{}$ pints of yellow paint for each pint of blue paint." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434582 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a00e84f9-44fd-5a43-a586-d42bdbf5d49a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434582 #edb/ref 1074 "The ratio of the number of pints of yellow paint to the pints of blue paint is  $5:6.$ \n\nWe can rewrite this ratio as a fraction, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{5}{6}\n$$\n\nThis means that there is $\\frac{5}{6}$ pint of yellow paint for each pint of blue paint." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434583 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186434569 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434583 #edb/ref 1069 "q-60292" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434583 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434583 #edb/ref 1071 "What is missing in the following sentence?\n\nColin and Emma shared some candies in the ratio of $6:4$, so there are $\\boxed{}$ candies in Colin's share for each candy in Emma's share." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434583 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a47458ac-762b-5c69-b95f-710fff05fa39" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434583 #edb/ref 1074 "We can rewrite the ratio as a fraction, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{6}{4}\n$$\n\nWe can simplify the fraction by dividing the numerator and denominator by $2$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{6}{4}=\\frac{6÷2}{4÷2}=\\frac{3}{2}\n$$\n\nThat means that there are $\\frac{3}{2}$ candies in Colin's share for each candy in Emma's share." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434584 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186434572 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434584 #edb/ref 1069 "q-60247" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434584 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434584 #edb/ref 1071 "From left to right, what are the missing numbers in the following sentence?\n\nIn beverage, there are $\\frac{1}{9}$ cups of honey for each cup of black tea. Therefore, the beverage has a ratio of $\\boxed{}$ cup of honey to $\\boxed{}$ cups of black tea." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434584 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "adc40226-3cff-5a2e-b82d-73ec328aa1c5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434584 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's rewrite the fraction $\\frac{1}{9}$ as a ratio:\n\n$$\n1:9\n$$\n\nTherefore, the beverage has a ratio of $1$ cup of honey to $9$ cups of black tea." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434585 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186434570 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434585 #edb/ref 1069 "q-60259" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434585 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434585 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/5f/5f12694252ed0263813d89a887a8a16e43db5f03d3c9bfdc566f3dccf2fa905b.png)\n\nIf the ratio of squares to total shapes is $\\frac{5}{\\boxed{}}$ then what is the missing number?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434585 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "df95efd6-f297-5326-bb25-68164061a5b0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434585 #edb/ref 1074 "We count the number of squares. We see that there are $5$ squares.\n\n We count the total number of shapes. We see that there are $8$ shapes.\n\nHence, the ratio of squares to total shapes is$\\frac{5}{8}$\n\nSo the missing number is $8.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434586 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186434571 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434586 #edb/ref 1069 "q-101463" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434586 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434586 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/12/120abe5f972927f0e33107f01f55ea8e03b5a229b7c252c79c409b89103a6e33.png)\n\nWhat ratio describes the number of triangles to the total number of shapes?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434586 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e3030ed1-6414-589f-94d2-632afe0b2f49" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434586 #edb/ref 1074 "We count the number of triangles. We see that there are $3$ triangles.\n\nWe count the total number of shapes. We see that there are $8$ shapes in total.\n\nSo the ratio of triangles to the total number of shapes is $\\frac{3}{8}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434587 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186434575 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434587 #edb/ref 1069 "q-60249" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434587 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434587 #edb/ref 1071 "From left to right, what are the missing numbers in the following sentence?\n\nIn a beverage, there are $\\frac{2}{7}$ teaspoons of ginger for each teaspoon of sugar. Therefore, the beverage has a ratio of $\\boxed{}$ teaspoons of ginger to $\\boxed{}$ teaspoons of sugar." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434587 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f0557329-924c-5116-b187-33f66bcdf532" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434587 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's rewrite the fraction $\\frac{2}{7}$ as a ratio:\n\n$$\n2:7\n$$\n\nTherefore, the beverage has a ratio of $2$ teaspoons of ginger to $7$ teaspoons of sugar." #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
